node` (a Capability that no longer matches never enters the conditional-
facet loop, so the facet-loop warn disappears), and five in this pass's
own `zero-affected-component-match` -- the last of these is worth
naming: under the intersection reading, `all([])` is vacuously true, so
EVERY Capability "matches" on zero affected components, which is exactly
the inverted answer REQ-006(g) exists to forbid. The new fixture
therefore discriminates this mutant on its own, independently of the
